+# S004 data model
+
+## Entities
+
+### Retry credit balance
+
+| Field | Meaning | Rules |
+|---|---|---|
+| `workspace_id` | Workspace that owns the quota. | Primary or unique key; all access is workspace-scoped. |
+| `available_credits` | Credits that may still be reserved. | Non-negative integer. |
+| `updated_at` | Last accounting mutation time. | Updated in the transaction that changes the balance. |
+
+### Retry reservation
+
+| Field | Meaning | Rules |
+|---|---|---|
+| `reservation_id` | Durable reservation identifier. | Primary key. |
+| `workspace_id` | Workspace charged by the attempt. | Must reference the same workspace as the balance. |
+| `attempt_key` | Stable key shared by dispatch and all terminal handlers. | Unique with `workspace_id`; duplicates return this record. |
+| `state` | `reserved`, `finalized`, or `released`. | Starts `reserved`; terminal states are immutable. |
+| `created_at` | Reservation time. | Set at successful reserve. |
+| `finalized_at` | Provider acceptance recorded. | Set only on `reserved → finalized`. |
+| `released_at` | Credit restored. | Set only on `reserved → released`. |
+| `terminal_reason` | `accepted`, `failed`, `timed_out`, or `cancelled`. | Required for terminal state; immutable once recorded. |
+
+## State machine
+
+```text
+                    provider accepted
+reserved --------------------------------> finalized
+   |
+   | provider failed, timed out, or cancelled
+   v
+released
+```
+
+- Only `reserved` can transition.
+- `finalized` and `released` are terminal. Repeated requests return the stored outcome and make no balance change.
+- If competing terminal handlers arrive, the transaction that first changes the row owns the outcome; the other observes and returns that outcome.
+
+## Invariants
+
+1. A reservation is created only in the same transaction that changes its workspace balance from `n` to `n - 1`, with `n > 0`.
+2. A release changes the balance from `n` to `n + 1` only in the same transaction that changes its reservation from `reserved` to `released`.
+3. Finalization changes no balance because the credit was consumed by the successful reservation.
+4. At most one reservation exists for a workspace and attempt key.
+5. No operation may observe or commit a negative `available_credits` value.
